### 2.2 Construction choice
**DOM/SVG single-stage scene (chosen):** one SVG; board rect; bowl group (outer wall ellipse + inner paste field); paste layer = paste ellipse whose coverage scales with pasteP + pasteDark texture blobs (seeded, positions derived from object index); objects layer — per object a group (die: rounded rect + pip circles · house: rect + roof polygon · minidie: small rect + dark pips · cube: rect) transformed by integrity (scale toward deformShrink floor then fleck, corner radius toward deformRound, fill blended toward paste, y sunk by sinkPx × (1−integrity), pips fading first); pestle group (ellipse head + handle rect) positioned by the stroke machine; three CONFIG label texts (input label fades as readableCount falls below half, output label fades in as pasteP passes its midpoint — label swap is a state readout, not a caption). All geometry from `stateAt(cfg,t)`, a pure function evaluable in node.
Rejected: Canvas 2D — loses per-element ink measurement the A6 fit leg needs. CSS keyframes — phase state not evaluable as a pure function (A11 receipts impossible). Photographic/generated imagery — approaches the specimen; the technique is the per-stroke identity loss, carried by geometry.
**Named deferrals (lawful, priced):** (1) Hands — not built; the pestle moves by its own stroke machine (fleet diagram form for performed-action techniques, T233 precedent). (2) The wide→close-up shot cut (1000–1500 ms) is compressed onto the single stage: the build's setup act shows the same bowl at stage scale throughout (no zoom); the census cut is a camera change, not a state change — the STATE at 1500 (full set, pestle raised) is what the build binds. (3) The prior technique's chess pieces (CP0/CP1 left foreground) — set dressing of T14, omitted. (4) Texture realism of the stone bowl/paste — flat CONFIG colours + seeded dark blobs stand in for photographic texture; the technique priced is the collapse law, not the material render.

