101:- **Census-count tension (named in §2.3):** the specimen's readable count at 3000/5000 ms runs ≈3–4 higher than a strict per-stroke integrity law gives, because partially mashed objects still read. Mitigation priced: integrity's readable threshold is 0.5 and deform (round/blend/sink) is progressive, so a mid-stroke object is visibly degraded — the motion/timing lenses judge the LAW's fidelity; if they price the count gap, the cure is a collapseSpan > 1 stroke (integrity loss spanning into the next stroke), named here as the first cure candidate.
102:- **Morph-vs-increment reading:** smooth per-object deform could read as a morph, betraying stop-motion. The stepMs quantization binds ALL mash motion to 120 ms increments; P7 asserts it executably.
103:- **Paste-coverage honesty:** coverage must come from collapsed fraction (Σ integrity), never an independent timeline — a paste that grows on its own clock while objects stay readable is the named defect; stateAt derives pasteP from the objects, by construction.
104:- **Fleck persistence:** collapsed objects must persist as colour flecks (the specimen's end state is flecked, not clean) — fleckCount = collapsed count, asserted at P5.
105:- **Label fitting:** longest labels ("DICE · HOUSES · CUBES" 21 chars at labelFontPx 30, swap "BUTTONS · BEADS · COINS" 23 chars) measured in the fit leg at the 360 px stage; a measured overflow is cured in CONFIG font size only.
106:- **Pestle occlusion:** at stroke bottoms the pestle head covers centre objects — in the specimen this is real occlusion; the build draws the pestle above the objects layer, priced as faithful.
107:- **Render-proof limitation:** no browser binary in this seat — PIXEL-UNVERIFIED carried to scores.md; comparison page is the render surface.
108:- **Plateau (A2):** FIRST ATTEMPT — no prior average. **Predicted minimum lens: motion fidelity** — hypothesis: the specimen's strokes are hand-driven circular grinds with irregular targets while the build's are a regular left→right sweep, and the census-count tension (§2.3) may also price there; if the wave's minimum is another lens, the WHY in scores.md names it.
